#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184065 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184167 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Statements Using the Vector Space Axioms"}] :question/id #uuid "2cb88713-f830-501e-9b0a-60320936ad14" :question/math-academy-id "e-4792" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\textrm A1] - [\\textrm A8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*If $\\mathbf{w}$ is a vector such that $\\mathbf{w}+\\mathbf{w} = \\mathbf{w}$, then $\\mathbf{w}=\\mathbf{0}.$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (w+w)+(-w) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{add [math]-\\mathbf{w}[/math] to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(w+(-w)) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the axioms of a vector space, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (w+w)+(-w) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{add [math]-\\mathbf{w}[/math] to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(w+(-w)) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom [math]{\\color{blue}\\text{A2}}[/math]}\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom [math]{\\color{blue}\\text{A3}}[/math]}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184094 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/id #uuid "132efc65-5f50-5582-8955-a5d34c57af04" :question/math-academy-id "e-8224" :question/problem "Let $V$ be the set of all real polynomials of degree exactly $3$, equipped with the usual addition and scalar multiplication operations. Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$V$ is **not** a vector space because $\\textrm{_________}\\,.$*\n\nI. the sum of two polynomials of degree $3$ may not be a polynomial of degree $3$\n\nII. $V$ does not contain the polynomial $-p(x)$ for every $p(x) \\in V$\n\nIII. addition of polynomials is not commutative" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer  is as follows:\n\n*$V$ is **not** a vector space because **the sum of two polynomials of degree $3$ may not be a polynomial of degree $3$.** *\n\nFor instance, if $p(x) = 1 +x^3$ and $q(x) = 1-x^3$, then $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ are in $V.$ However  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x)+q(x) & =(1+{x}^{3})+(1-{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =2\\notin V.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative.\n\n- For any polynomial $p(x)$ of degree $3$, the corresponding negative polynomial $-p(x)$ also has degree $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243958 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c2c12e0-1cd2-57dc-bb2e-fccfbfe29b6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in F$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242269} {:answer/id #uuid "aed90e2c-7d1b-5ac3-9ce4-8c895e1d0385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of functions in $F$ do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242706} {:answer/id #uuid "c9bc4983-8538-5113-9d78-363014648f95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of $f,g\\in F$ is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242959} {:answer/id #uuid "cdb145c6-2092-56d4-9ff1-6bbe59e69ca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of $f,g\\in F$ is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242990} {:answer/id #uuid "d3235266-f3fb-58a4-8cd7-6dda3548ef28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$F$ does not contain the zero element" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3235266-f3fb-58a4-8cd7-6dda3548ef28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$F$ does not contain the zero element" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243041} :answer-field/id #uuid "39664c8c-a6d4-545a-b91d-30b8ab061a3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fe3a1a04-348a-505c-9183-5288567e7407" :question/math-academy-id "q-106813" :question/problem "Let $F$ be the set of functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$F$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$F$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because **$F$ does not contain the zero element.** *\n\nIndeed, evaluating the zero function $f(x)=0$ at $x=0,$ we have $f(0)=0\\ne \\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of $f,g\\in F$ is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of $f,g\\in F$ is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in F.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of functions satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442958 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42ef8948-2af5-570c-9086-ec884dd8b607" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1\\cdot (x,y)\\ne (x,y)$ for some $(x,y)\\in P$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442943} {:answer/id #uuid "6a2c8125-7050-51a6-849e-7893b298fda5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "there exists an ordered pair $(x,y)\\in P$ such that $(x,y)+({x}^{′},{y}^{′})\\ne (0,0)$ for any $({x}^{′},{y}^{′})\\in P$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442944} {:answer/id #uuid "a00c70d5-ced0-52ad-b2b1-04b1b14b6676" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of ordered pairs in $P$ is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442946} {:answer/id #uuid "cc589644-69c0-5cf3-a95d-7450d4d2431d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplication by a scalar is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442950} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e42310-8e15-5635-82fb-c6e17cfba1a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ does not contain the zero element" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a00c70d5-ced0-52ad-b2b1-04b1b14b6676" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of ordered pairs in $P$ is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442946} :answer-field/id #uuid "657d2f5e-8283-512c-8736-a6b6bb9a9cf9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d3e3740-f421-5f05-912d-ea42f86d4dd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-106816" :question/problem "Let $P$ be the set of all ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ such that $xy=0.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$P$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to the usual component-wise addition and scalar multiplication in ${R}^{2}$) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$P$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to the usual component-wise addition and scalar multiplication in ${R}^{2}$) because **addition of ordered pairs in $P$ is not closed.** *  \n\nFor example, $(1,0)\\in P$ because $1\\cdot 0=0$ and $(0,1)\\in P$ because $0\\cdot 1=0.$ However, if we add the two pairs component-wise, we get\n\n$$\n(1,0)+(0,1)=(1+0,0+1)=(1,1).\n$$\n\nThe product of the components of this pair is $1\\cdot 1=1\\ne 0.$ So, $(1,0)+(0,1)\\notin P.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Multiplication of $(x,y)\\in P$ by a scalar is closed. Indeed, if $\\alpha \\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\alpha \\cdot (x,y)=(\\alpha x,\\alpha y)\\in P\n$$\n\nsince $(\\alpha x)\\cdot (\\alpha y)={\\alpha }^{2}{{(xy)}_{⏟}}_{=0}=0.$\n$\\,✓$\n\n- The zero element in $P$ is $(0,0).$ $✓$\n\n- For an ordered pair $(x,y)\\in P,$ the ordered pair $-(x,y)=(-x,-y)$ is also an element of $P$ since $(-x)\\cdot (-y)=xy=0.$\n$\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot (x,y)=(x,y)$ for all $(x,y)\\in P.$ $\\,✓$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184167 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Statements Using the Vector Space Axioms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37f895bf-32a0-582a-8d97-d103675f97d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382856} {:answer/id #uuid "1424205e-d67d-53ee-af7a-6ddb217cbfbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382857} {:answer/id #uuid "46cd3b22-e386-5fa6-aabd-63ef9e1e4cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382858} {:answer/id #uuid "d28fa3e4-82e9-57ec-9bf4-a7fe05ccb798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382859} {:answer/id #uuid "bb3c69bb-91a9-5d18-87bf-5b38f0a772a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A5}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1424205e-d67d-53ee-af7a-6ddb217cbfbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382857} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfb87e51-0939-50f0-9aed-8dbfbe993c59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e00386b5-a859-5a68-9df5-ac8710a4ede8" :question/math-academy-id "q-106942" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*If $u$ and $v$ are vectors such that $u+x=v+x$ for some $x\\in V,$ then $u=v.$*\n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u+x & =v+x &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (u+x)+(-x) & =(v+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ u+(x+(-x)) & =v+(x+(-x)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ u+0 & =v+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ u & =v &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u+x & =v+x &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (u+x)+(-x) & =(v+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ u+(x+(-x)) & =v+(x+(-x)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ u+0 & =v+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A4}\\,] \\\\ u & =v &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399587 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184167 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Statements Using the Vector Space Axioms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96cab4fe-b011-5072-be3e-391125bf75c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399589} {:answer/id #uuid "479eb2f9-8717-57b1-9f07-9c964bbfdbab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A7}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399590} {:answer/id #uuid "fcde83fb-02ab-5892-a45a-6c4b43adb9eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A7}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399591} {:answer/id #uuid "e44c72a4-6813-558a-a34c-560c1aff92da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399592} {:answer/id #uuid "afcd5ca7-6625-5f48-ac5f-5ce7f390cf1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A6}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e44c72a4-6813-558a-a34c-560c1aff92da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399592} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fb9d1c7-c909-596f-a04a-7d5c7e74340d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399588}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "258def85-3c26-5841-81d2-c1a1f3c916a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-106944" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*$0\\cdot 0=0$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =(0+1)\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A7}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{addition of integers}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A5}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A5}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =(0+1)\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A7}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{addition of integers}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A5}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184761 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30f17da9-a2bd-5534-adad-c7eb18896578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W$ does not contain the zero element" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321524} {:answer/id #uuid "40484eb7-546a-59c5-8075-7334001f71a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321654} {:answer/id #uuid "63232a3a-2f7e-5f2a-8880-e7b2f5f26a0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of polynomials is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321919} {:answer/id #uuid "77129de6-3842-5621-aee0-6e8854935738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of polynomials is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322079} {:answer/id #uuid "dec5bb24-cf51-550f-854c-ba44585b5dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W$ does not contain the polynomial $-p(x)$ for every $p(x)\\in W$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30f17da9-a2bd-5534-adad-c7eb18896578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W$ does not contain the zero element" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321524} :answer-field/id #uuid "f229d374-9057-5731-87e8-a3f0484852d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323648}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ac2c9af3-5c5a-5bc3-898a-7e78bc1b3b9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-35558" :question/problem "Let $W$ be the set of all polynomials in the variable $x\\in R$ with coefficients in $R$ of degree $5$ or greater. Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$W$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$W$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because **$W$ does not contain the zero element.** *\n\nIndeed, the zero polynomial has degree $0$, which is less than $5.$\n\nOn the other hand: \n\n- Addition of polynomials is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- For any polynomial $p(x)$ of degree $5$ (or greater), the corresponding negative polynomial $-p(x)$ has the same degree. $\\,✓$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385324 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184167 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Statements Using the Vector Space Axioms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1337dd4f-9280-53a2-a0bf-10fa5a1172ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385326} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b06213-6b70-5fb1-9074-bd29c49e8d32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385327} {:answer/id #uuid "175edfb7-a947-56df-a366-83319bf965d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385328} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4ae0dc-f023-5eac-8d6f-6539fcd8b68a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A5}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385329} {:answer/id #uuid "f383b979-fa8e-5c2b-8977-e24abfd545ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "175edfb7-a947-56df-a366-83319bf965d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385328} :answer-field/id #uuid "6de75fa4-40ed-54ed-9a38-aaf2ba31ee58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c7e8b0d2-1b58-5e69-8702-c53196883e47" :question/math-academy-id "q-35627" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Given any $x\\in V$, if $w$ is a vector such that $x+w=0$, then $w=-x$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442957 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184167 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Statements Using the Vector Space Axioms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fb37ed3-36ac-5e3f-851e-4f837d79e1fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A6}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442941} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4204de-6303-5664-ae87-4bb545b11579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A8}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442942} {:answer/id #uuid "bd7ca824-8d41-582d-8e53-440a67967f94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A7}$, $\\text{A1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442948} {:answer/id #uuid "d0cc0d55-4b7a-527b-8c30-4752964eae4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A5}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442951} {:answer/id #uuid "d1440eed-dbe7-537c-9d9e-09e10d43a8a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a4204de-6303-5664-ae87-4bb545b11579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A8}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442942} :answer-field/id #uuid "700b38c9-75a1-52e4-bc40-89a679395057" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442955}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2473766c-4484-58b4-94f0-d8e70773f841" :question/math-academy-id "q-35629" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:* \n\n*$\\alpha 0=0$ for any $\\alpha \\in R$*\n\n*Proof:* \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha 0 & =\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0 & =\\alpha (0+0) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0 & =\\alpha 0+\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0+(-\\alpha 0) & =(\\alpha 0+\\alpha 0)+(-\\alpha 0) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-\\alpha 0\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0+(-\\alpha 0) & =\\alpha 0+(\\alpha 0+(-\\alpha 0)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =\\alpha 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0 & =\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha 0 & =\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0 & =\\alpha (0+0) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0 & =\\alpha 0+\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A8}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0-\\alpha 0 & =(\\alpha 0+\\alpha 0)-\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{add }-\\alpha 0\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0-\\alpha 0 & =\\alpha 0+(\\alpha 0-\\alpha 0) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =\\alpha 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A4}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cf95fce-46b3-5fe1-926b-157ab6915f04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If $A\\in V$ then $-A\\notin V$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442939} {:answer/id #uuid "11142ab4-ada0-51aa-ab0b-0e0d13397eb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of matrices in $V$ is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442940} {:answer/id #uuid "7d8749ff-5a89-5515-91b1-92f223a41f80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of matrices in $V$ is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442945} {:answer/id #uuid "b58a38fd-ec79-5101-86b4-974746234698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the $2\\times 2$ zero matrix  is not in $V$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442947} {:answer/id #uuid "c34ae4c7-6893-5a03-b0ce-39213abac829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix  is not in $V$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b58a38fd-ec79-5101-86b4-974746234698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the $2\\times 2$ zero matrix  is not in $V$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442947} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1c519c6-ee9a-53ca-a030-5c374bc6f933" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "836e7d2e-0ac3-5b0c-b2c3-d01db384e22c" :question/math-academy-id "q-43858" :question/problem "Let $V$ be the set of all  $2\\times 2$ invertible matrices with real entries, with the usual matrix addition and scalar multiplication. Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$V$ is **not** a vector space  because $\\text{____}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is \n\n*$V$ is **not** a vector space  because **the $2\\times 2$ zero matrix is not in $V.$** *\n\nIndeed, the zero matrix doesn't have an inverse, so it doesn't belong to $V.$ As a result, $V$ cannot be a vector space.\n\nOn the other hand, \n\n- Addition of matrices is associative.  $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of matrices is commutative.  $\\,✓$\n\n- The $2\\times 2$ identity matrix is invertible, so it belongs to $V.$  $\\,✓$\n\n- If $A$ is invertible then $-A$ is invertible too. So, $-A\\in V.$ $\\,✓$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344968 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184167 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Statements Using the Vector Space Axioms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "360cc03a-3f39-5879-9a88-a61073b7fcf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342683} {:answer/id #uuid "6d6880fc-5f2b-5192-95d6-4d52a478dfb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343177} {:answer/id #uuid "71d6a532-cd4b-5d34-ae27-3901b1065d79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343222} {:answer/id #uuid "ca10db7b-bf57-5c5b-a421-62ab3bb870b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344014} {:answer/id #uuid "ea3d0561-a8a8-5898-828f-77cac082232d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A8}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "360cc03a-3f39-5879-9a88-a61073b7fcf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342683} :answer-field/id #uuid "86bd575b-d1b5-591b-a355-2d1fcad9bf66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c4dc6297-c39f-58c6-a8af-023dc6a275e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-74671" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*If $x$ is a vector such that $-x+w=w$ for some $w\\in V$, then $x=0$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ x+(-x+w) & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{adding }x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (x+(-x))+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{adding }-w\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+(w+(-w)) &  & [\\,\\text{axioms  A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ x+(-x+w) & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{adding }x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (x+(-x))+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{adding }-w\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+(w+(-w)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A4}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1a276ce-4807-5595-9e74-b4e01dcf3dbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition in $Y$ is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385833} {:answer/id #uuid "3910c94e-c1f6-54fb-9ca1-a7cfaec57a1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplication of $(x,y)\\in Y$ by a scalar is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385834} {:answer/id #uuid "7f241a5e-8166-53bb-b6ac-146d6e0797cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Y$ does not contain the zero element" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385835} {:answer/id #uuid "19ee9131-fd45-5cda-a995-429bb87fe4a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication in $Y$  do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385836} {:answer/id #uuid "c7ee2446-901d-5280-8a07-74ae51b172c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition in $Y$ is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3910c94e-c1f6-54fb-9ca1-a7cfaec57a1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplication of $(x,y)\\in Y$ by a scalar is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385834} :answer-field/id #uuid "a767cfd0-5f8e-59db-8dfc-c580d16b2f17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96e3d27f-a6f3-58f8-a748-ec53b79d0713" :question/math-academy-id "q-94808" :question/problem "Let $Y$ be the set of all ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$  such that $x+y\\le 3.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to the usual component-wise addition and scalar multiplication in ${R}^{2}$) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to the usual component-wise addition and scalar multiplication in ${R}^{2}$) because **multiplication of $(x,y)\\in Y$ by a scalar is not closed.** *  \n\nFor example, $(1,1)\\in Y$ because $1+1=2\\le 3.$ However, if we add the components of $2\\cdot (1,1)=(2,2),$ we get $2+2=4>3.$ So, $2\\cdot (1,1)\\notin Y.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition in $Y$ is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- The zero element in $Y$ is $(0,0).$ $✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication in $Y$ satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition in $Y$ is commutative. $\\,✓$"}]}
